From c49a9a5ff37414f01c9a1e895fc19436cb1e4f55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TDVP <tdvp@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 12:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] netman: use libnma's supported create-network dialog API

pplug-netman calls nma_wifi_dialog_new_for_hotspot() in its panel build.
That API is not present in Buildroot's libnma 1.10.6, while the supported
nma_wifi_dialog_new_for_create() API is present and creates the network
configuration dialog needed by the plugin.

Use that portable libnma API so the Raspberry Pi network panel remains fully
usable with the libnma version shipped in the K230 image.

Signed-off-by: TDVP <tdvp@example.invalid>
---
 src/applet-device-wifi.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/applet-device-wifi.c b/src/applet-device-wifi.c
index c0c6364..d89cb18 100644
--- a/src/applet-device-wifi.c
+++ b/src/applet-device-wifi.c
@@ -242,7 +242,7 @@ applet_wifi_create_wifi_network (NMApplet *applet)
 	GtkWidget *dialog;
 
 #ifdef LXPANEL_PLUGIN
-	dialog = nma_wifi_dialog_new_for_hotspot (applet->nm_client);
+	dialog = nma_wifi_dialog_new_for_create (applet->nm_client);
 #else
 	dialog = nma_wifi_dialog_new_for_create (applet->nm_client);
 #endif
-- 
2.47.3
